\begin{abstract}
The Superluminal Thermodynamics Simulation Engine (STSE-H v2.0) is a 
production-grade computational framework for evaluating warp-field metric 
deformation, tachyonic thermodynamics, and extended ADM 3+1 Hamiltonian 
constraints under superluminal velocity regimes. Real astrophysical datasets 
(Gaia DR3, Planck 2018, LIGO transients) are integrated directly into a 
GPU-accelerated solver architecture secured by AES-GCM-256 hardware enclaves. 
Automated warp-factor sweeping and encrypted telemetry logging enable 
high-fidelity stress testing up to Warp~3375, demonstrating stable manifold 
behavior with Hamiltonian violation below $6.42\times10^{-14}$.
\end{abstract}

